---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Book Drew Reitzel to Speak" description="Book Drew Reitzel for your church, conference, or event. Teaching on divided allegiance, cultural compromise, and the call back to undivided loyalty.">
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="section-padding bg-black">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-4xl">
      <div class="fade-in">
        <span class="text-red text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] block mb-6">Speaking</span>
        <h1 class="mb-6">Bring the Message to Your Community</h1>
        <div class="divider mb-6"></div>
        <p class="text-muted-light text-xl leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
          Drew is available for churches, conferences, retreats, and events
          where biblical truth is the standard, not the exception.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Message -->
  <section class="section-padding bg-charcoal">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-4xl fade-in">
      <h2 class="mb-4">The Message</h2>
      <div class="divider mb-12"></div>
      <div class="space-y-6 max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-muted-light text-lg leading-relaxed">
          Most of us are not running from God. We are just divided. We show up on Sunday and fight
          the same fight all week, giving Jesus some and the world the rest, and wondering why we
          feel so tired.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed">
          Drew Reitzel takes the hardest line Jesus ever drew, Matthew 6:24, and uses it to set
          people free. He speaks with real love for the people who are still deciding which master
          they serve, and he is still in the fight himself, which is the point. A room leaves with
          the quiet exhaustion of a divided heart named out loud, and with an invitation home.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Topics -->
  <section class="section-padding bg-black">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-4xl fade-in">
      <h2 class="mb-4">Speaking Topics</h2>
      <div class="divider mb-12"></div>
      <div class="space-y-8">
        {[
          {
            title: 'You Can\'t Serve Two Masters',
            description: 'The exhaustion of the divided life and the freedom of one allegiance. Where the pull between what we were made for and everything else competing for that place actually comes from, and the one decision that ends it.',
          },
          {
            title: 'Who Needs to Hear This?',
            description: 'Loving the divided home, what it costs and why it is worth it. For the husband, wife, parent or friend who loves someone pulled in two directions and has run out of things to say.',
          },
          {
            title: 'The Invitation Inside Matthew 6:24',
            description: 'The hardest line Jesus drew and the invitation hidden inside it. Built for a Sunday morning or a retreat session, and written to send people home with something they can act on that week.',
          },
          {
            title: 'The Church Is Choosing',
            description: 'Why the American Church\'s departure from biblical truth is not accidental, and what it will take to return.',
          },
        ].map((topic) => (
          <div class="p-8 bg-charcoal border-l-2 border-red">
            <h3 class="text-xl mb-3">{topic.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed">{topic.description}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Formats -->
  <section class="section-padding bg-charcoal">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-4xl fade-in">
      <h2 class="mb-4">Formats</h2>
      <div class="divider mb-12"></div>
      <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        Sunday morning services. Men's gatherings. Conferences. Retreats. Seminars. Drew works with
        the shape of your event rather than asking your event to fit a talk, and he is glad to talk
        through what would serve your people before anything is booked.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- For Hosts -->
  <section class="section-padding bg-black">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-4xl fade-in">
      <h2 class="mb-4">For Podcast and Radio Hosts</h2>
      <div class="divider mb-12"></div>
      <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-8">
        Drew is available for interviews, and these are the three conversations that tend to serve
        an audience best.
      </p>
      <div class="space-y-8">
        {[
          {
            title: 'The most exhausting way to live',
            description: 'Why a divided heart, rather than a hard life, is what wears people out, and the one decision that ends it.',
          },
          {
            title: 'You can\'t argue someone home',
            description: 'How to reach the people you love who are pulled in two, without preaching at them or pushing them away.',
          },
          {
            title: 'The verse nobody wants to preach',
            description: 'Matthew 6:24 as Jesus meant it, what undivided allegiance asks, and what it gives back.',
          },
        ].map((angle) => (
          <div class="p-8 bg-charcoal border-l-2 border-red">
            <h3 class="text-xl mb-3">{angle.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed">{angle.description}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- About Drew -->
  <section class="section-padding bg-charcoal">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-4xl fade-in">
      <h2 class="mb-4">About Drew</h2>
      <div class="divider mb-12"></div>
      <div class="space-y-6 max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed">
          Drew Reitzel writes about the most uncomfortable truth in American Christianity: that you
          cannot give Jesus part of your life and the world the rest. He is 61, a New Yorker, and
          direct. He says it with real love for people who are still deciding which master they
          serve.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed">
          His book, <a href="/book/" class="text-red hover:underline">You Can't Serve Two Masters:
          Undivided Allegiance To Christ In An Age of Cultural Compromise</a>, names the quiet
          exhaustion of a divided heart and calls the reader home with compassion. It is written for
          the person who loves God and still feels pulled in two directions, and for the people who
          love that person and do not know what to say.
          <a href="/about/" class="text-red hover:underline">More about Drew</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Inquiry Form -->
  <section class="section-padding bg-black">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-2xl fade-in">
      <h2 class="text-center mb-4">Request Drew to Speak</h2>
      <div class="divider mx-auto mb-6"></div>
      <p class="text-muted text-center leading-relaxed mb-12">
        Tell us about your event and Drew will come back to you himself.
      </p>

      <form class="space-y-6" data-speaking-form>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div>
            <label class="block text-sm text-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Name</label>
            <input
              type="text"
              name="name"
              required
              class="w-full px-4 py-3 bg-charcoal border border-cream/10 text-cream placeholder:text-muted focus:outline-none focus:border-red transition-colors"
            />
          </div>
          <div>
            <label class="block text-sm text-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Email</label>
            <input
              type="email"
              name="email"
              required
              class="w-full px-4 py-3 bg-charcoal border border-cream/10 text-cream placeholder:text-muted focus:outline-none focus:border-red transition-colors"
            />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <label class="block text-sm text-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Organization / Church</label>
          <input
            type="text"
            name="organization"
            class="w-full px-4 py-3 bg-charcoal border border-cream/10 text-cream placeholder:text-muted focus:outline-none focus:border-red transition-colors"
          />
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div>
            <label class="block text-sm text-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Event Type</label>
            <select name="event_type" class="w-full px-4 py-3 bg-charcoal border border-cream/10 text-cream focus:outline-none focus:border-red transition-colors">
              <option value="">Select type</option>
              <option value="church">Church Service</option>
              <option value="conference">Conference</option>
              <option value="retreat">Retreat</option>
              <option value="seminar">Seminar</option>
              <option value="other">Other</option>
            </select>
          </div>
          <div>
            <label class="block text-sm text-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Preferred Date</label>
            <input
              type="date"
              name="date"
              class="w-full px-4 py-3 bg-charcoal border border-cream/10 text-cream focus:outline-none focus:border-red transition-colors"
            />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <label class="block text-sm text-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Message</label>
          <textarea
            name="message"
            rows="5"
            class="w-full px-4 py-3 bg-charcoal border border-cream/10 text-cream placeholder:text-muted focus:outline-none focus:border-red transition-colors resize-none"
            placeholder="Tell us about your event..."
          ></textarea>
        </div>

        <button type="submit" class="btn-primary w-full justify-center">
          Submit Inquiry
        </button>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
